		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5097&amp;p=36973#p36973"><![CDATA[
I'm running Win11 (up to date) and the OGD77 CPS 2025.03.23.01 CPS.  I'm trying to update the radio Firmware in my TYT MDUV390 GPS from 20240803 to 20240908 version.  I put the radio in DFU mode but it appears in device manager as USB mode.  Specifically, if I just turn on the radio, it appears in the Ports section as OpenGD77 (COM3) and I can upload and download to/from it.  If I turn it off, put it in DFU mode, it then appears under Other Devices as a "Digital Radio in USB mode".  So the CPS gives an error message saying no radio in DFU mode is attached.<br><br>This isn't the first update I've done and in the past so long as the CPS saw the radio in USB mode, once I put it in DFU mode, the CPS saw it as such and uploaded the firmware.<br><br>Any clues to a way to fix this?<br><br>Steve<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5794">W3ATN</a> — Fri May 02, 2025 8:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
